; Stag — model scene for AnimalDefinition.model_scenes.
; Source: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack" (July 2021), CC0 1.0 — same pack as
; Fox; see project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
;
; Design role: decided substitute for the Leopard gap (art.md → Newly Available Animals /
; Desired Roster Assets — Still Missing) as well as a first-class roster candidate in its
; own right (art.md → Newly Available Animals: forest, cover, rocks · Shy, "trophy").
;
; Audit (2026-07-26): 13 animation clips confirmed on the raw glTF — Idle, Idle_2,
; Idle_Headlow, Idle_HitReact1/2, Walk, Gallop, Gallop_Jump, Jump_toIdle, Eating,
; Attack_Headbutt, Attack_Kick, Death. Idle/Walk both present and non-degenerate (42
; tracks each). Node structure matches Fox (AnimalArmature -> Skeleton3D -> mesh(es);
; AnimationPlayer sibling index 1) except for one extra piece: the antlers are a separate
; "Stag_Horns" MeshInstance3D on a BoneAttachment3D under the Head bone, riding along with
; the base mesh automatically — no extra wiring needed in this wrapper.
;
; Scale: 0.2, matching Fox's established factor for this exact pack (same rationale as
; Deer.tscn). Raw AABB height 5.378 -> scaled height 1.076, the tallest of the 9 new
; imports — plausible for a stag (biggest animal in the "deer" family here) but FLAG FOR
; HUMAN REVIEW alongside Deer/Alpaca: not yet eyeball-confirmed against the rest of the
; roster at the same table.
